{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1097528-time-travel-in-the-continuum","id":1097528,"title":"Time Travel in the Continuum","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-27T08:21:57-07:00","id":1097528,"title":"Time Travel in the Continuum","content":"I was wondering if there would be rules for time traveling in the Continuum? Maybe in a setting past Aeon. I believe Max Mercer was the only one that did it in the original game. I've been inspired by the likes of the fantastic 12 Monkeys TV show, the not so fantastic Legends of Tomorrow, and an RPG from the 90s called, &quot;Continuum.&quot; I'm sure the name is just coincidence. I'm afraid that the &quot;time keeping&quot; as it were could become overly daunting to keep up with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T08:43:36-07:00","id":1097535,"title":"","content":"I believe originally time travel as only ever present in the Aberrant Player's Guide, and there, it only gave a few rough guidelines. No canon characters ever used or developed the ability besides Max Mercer to my knowledge.<br /> <br /> I hold the view that time travel is fine conceptually once we get more of the Continuum hammered out. There are a couple of models presented in the Aberrant Player's Guide, but ultimately I think we should try for a framework that best allows cool time travel adventures. Really, what lets players do the most cool stuff should always be the focus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T09:16:06-07:00","id":1097548,"title":"","content":"Ian's mentioned having plans on handling time travel and alternate timelines somewhere down the line - not in the core TC book, but he's pretty sure he knows where he'll put them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T00:30:29-07:00","id":1098010,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/diving-into-the-continuum-trinity-continuum/\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty sure it is part of the base concept; there is no one history, but an endless continuum. </a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}